=== W8: Forward and reverse lineage ===
graph/mod.rs provides:
- out_edges(db, node): all edges from node (line 61)
- in_edges(db, node): all edges to node (line 76)
- neighbours(db, seed, depth): undirected neighbourhood BFS (line 93)
- impact_set(db, seeds, depth): deterministic impact traversal (line 133)

Full forward lineage: outcome/feature -> scenario -> requirement -> decision -> architecture -> task -> code -> test -> evidence -> release is traceable through EDGE_TYPES: REALISES, GOVERNED_BY, VALIDATES, TESTS, IMPLEMENTS, DEPENDS_ON, etc.

Reverse impact: impact_set uses IMPACT_IN (nodes reaching X through these in-edge types: DEPENDS_ON, IMPLEMENTS, REALISES, GOVERNED_BY, TESTS, USES, CONSUMES, GENERATED_FROM, DERIVED_FROM, IMPORTS, CALLS) and IMPACT_OUT (AFFECTS, BLOCKS, CONSTRAINS, VALIDATED_BY, PRODUCES, SUPERSEDES).

Missing lineage: dangling_edges detects edges to non-existent nodes.
Stale lineage: supersession tracked via SUPERSEDES edges; staleness field on records.

PASS: All W8 bullets evidenced.
